{
  "_comment": "Weapon attachments (§4.2, §5.1, §5.6.3). Each one changes a number the combat model already reads: MOA off the group, seconds off §5.3's settling, rounds onto the magazine, or a multiplier onto §5.6.1's noise. attaches_to lists calibres, so a fit is decided by the same string that decides whether ammunition fits — a typo makes an attachment useless rather than universal. These are the rarest things in the game on purpose: §5.6.3 calls the suppressor a change in how the game is played rather than a percentage, and the same is true of the rest. Crafting them needs a high Engineering skill (§7), which is why craft_skill is here rather than in a recipe file — the item states its own price.",
